From 7f81b965be95e9e40c2776d1d5cdc0bcf8e1df1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:31:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] CUDA: fold the q8_1 quantization of an activation into
 the norm producing it

Port of the R9700/HIP track patch 0009 ("CUDA/HIP: fold the q8_1
quantization of an activation into the norm producing it", Claude Fable 5).
The norm kernel registers the quantization in the per-graph cache under
exactly the tuple ggml_cuda_mul_mat_vec_q would use, so consumers skip their
own quantize launch.

CUDA-specific change: the cache's insert() takes no pool here, because cached
buffers come from the graph-scoped slab introduced by this track's dedupe
patch (the CUDA VMM pool is a strict LIFO stack). The registration helper
already treats a nullptr return as "do not fold", which is exactly what a
slab-full miss produces, so the fallback path is unchanged.
